## Note
The East Asian Width property of codepoint `r` as a code (`N`, `Na`, `A`, `W`, `H`, `F`) (`unicodedata.east_asian_width`).

Codepoints outside the table default to `N`; the lookup binary-searches the width range table.

## To unicodedataEastAsianWidth (r: Int) -> Text:
    Let tbl be unicodeEawTable().
    Let cnt be (length of tbl) / 3.
    Let mutable lo be 0.
    Let mutable hi be cnt - 1.
    Let mutable code be 0.
    While lo is at most hi:
        Let mid be (lo + hi) / 2.
        Let s be item ((mid * 3) + 1) of tbl.
        Let e be item ((mid * 3) + 2) of tbl.
        If r is less than s:
            Set hi to mid - 1.
        Otherwise:
            If r is greater than e:
                Set lo to mid + 1.
            Otherwise:
                Set code to item ((mid * 3) + 3) of tbl.
                Set lo to hi + 1.
    Let names be ["N", "Na", "A", "W", "H", "F"].
    Return item (code + 1) of names.
